# Privacy Policy

The Pi-hole Browser Extension needs access to the current browser tab and to the Pi-hole addresses configured by the user in order to provide its core functionality.

## Data processed

- The current domain is sent to the configured Pi-hole instances for status checks and whitelist or blacklist actions.
- The Pi-hole address and authentication information are sent only to the corresponding configured Pi-hole instance.
- Pi-hole connection details, preferences and temporary-action state are stored locally in the browser's extension storage and are not placed in browser synchronization storage.

## Data sharing

The extension does not send user data to the developers, analytics services or unrelated third parties. It does not use telemetry or advertising services. Network requests made for Pi-hole control are directed only to addresses explicitly configured by the user.

Links opened by the user, such as the GitHub issue tracker, donation page or uninstall survey, are external websites and are governed by their respective privacy policies.

